    "title": "Savannah Bananas take over Kenan Stadium in Chapel Hill",
    "text": "CHAPEL HILL, N.C. (WNCN) — The Savannah Bananas will be taking over Chapel Hill this weekend. The sold-out games are expected to bring in 50,000 people for each game on Saturday and Sunday at Kenan Stadium. According to Laurie Paolicelli of the Chapel Hill and Orange County Visitor Bureau, this is the first time Chapel Hill has hosted a large scale event back to back, which will be an economic boost for all of central North Carolina. “It’s an amazing weekend and it’s a first for us,” she said. “A lot of these guests are booking in Raleigh, Wake, Alamance,” she said. “It’s really exciting Chapel Hill and Kenan Stadium are an economic boom for the whole Triangle.” Small businesses like Chapel Hill Sportswear are taking advantage of the opportunity with yellow Carolina shirts. “Who doesn’t love yellow?” said Mattie York of Chapel Hill Sportswear. “It’s just such a happy color.” Saturday activities will begin at 2 p.m. and end around 10 p.m. Sunday events begin at 10 a.m. and end around 6 p.m. Each day, there will be a pre-game festival on Stadium Drive. Town officials recommend that attendees arrive to campus a few hours before the game to avoid traffic. MORE FROM CBS 17 ORANGE COUNTY NEWS “Get some lunch, get some drinks before you go to the stadium,” Chapel Hill Business Vitality manager Sarah Potter said. “It’s a really quick walk from downtown.” The Tar Heel Express will provide shuttle services from local park and ride lots to the event entrance along South Road. Information on parking can be found here.",
